    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 the full suite is green (47 tests, 0 failures/errors), including the new `Cp34Tests` age-band test.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the optional `birthDate` field with derived `ageBand` on the `POST /api/owners` create endpoint (read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added optional `birthDate` (ISO `date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema, and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` classes.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on the hsqldb schema with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be declared explicitly.\n4. **`AgeBands.java`** (new mapper helper) \u2014 computes the band from completed years between `birthDate` and `registrationDate` (`< 18` MINOR, `18\u201364` ADULT, `65+` SENIOR), returning `null` when `birthDate` is absent.\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `ageBand` via a MapStruct expression; `birthDate` maps by name automatically both in and out.\n\nThe request `birthDate` flows in through the existing `BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner` pipeline (MapStruct's `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`), is persisted, and `ageBand` is derived at response time against the owner's `registrationDate` \u2014 consistent whether served straight after creation or reloaded via GET.",
